   What to look at, and what "working" looks like:

     Courses      three subjects, and their version states differ on purpose. The hygiene course shows
                  a frozen Published version beside an editable Draft; the fire-safety one has only a
                  draft, and could not be assigned -- the seed printed that refusal above. A course
                  this world already carried was adopted rather than duplicated, so running this again
                  changes nothing on the screen instead of doubling it.
     Assignments  one role-scoped, two person-scoped, and Nora Berg's is OVERDUE by three days.
     Completions  four rows for three people. Jonas Lie has TWO: 55 % (failed) and 88 %
                  (passed), against a threshold of 80 %. The failed one is still there, because
                  the table is append-only and a retake is a new row.
     Certificates Expired / Expiring / Valid / Valid-forever, all four derived from the expiry date
                  against the store's calendar date. None of them blocks anything -- by design.
     Holdings     ask for Nora Berg: they hold 'alkoholservering' because they PASSED the course carrying
                  that key. Ask for Jonas Lie: they hold it too, on the retake -- and their expired
                  hygiene certificate is simply absent, never reported as a failure.

   What is NOT here, and is not a seeding gap:

     * No worker surface. All 16 routes are management under /training/stores/{storeId};
       /training/me/* does not exist, so nobody attests their own training and every completion reads
       ManagerRecorded. TrainingCompletionSource.Quiz is declared and written by no production code.
     * No onboarding, no checklists, no deviations -- the module's W2/W3 tables, none of which exist.
       Their flags are withheld from the operator catalog rather than offered as switches that do
       nothing: step 11 prints the refusal. docs/plans/PENDING-MIGRATIONS-LEDGER.md has the schema.
     * No reminders. training.reminders is withheld too; there is no dispatcher behind it.
     * No competency warning on the schedule. That is the module's headline differentiator and it is
       NOT wired -- see docs/plans/PROOF-BENCHMARKS.md, TR-B5.
